  },
  "name": "Generate product datasheets (spec sheets) from Google Sheets with ShipPDF",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "d0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -368,
        -256
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 760,
        "content": "# \ud83d\udea2 ShipPDF \u2014 Product datasheets on autopilot\n\n![ShipPDF](https://shippdf.com/assets/boat-mascot.png)\n\nTurn a product catalog in Google Sheets into branded **product datasheets / spec sheets** \u2014 one PDF per product, rendered by ShipPDF from your own reusable template.\n\n### How it works\n\n1. A new product row in Google Sheets triggers the workflow.\n2. ShipPDF renders a branded datasheet (spec table, description, optional product photo) from your template. The workflow **polls** until it's ready \u2014 so it runs on any n8n, Cloud or self-hosted, with no public callback URL.\n3. The finished PDF is archived to Google Drive.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Add a **ShipPDF API** credential (HTTP Bearer Auth, your key with `documents:create` + `documents:read`) and select it on both **Post Datasheet to ShipPDF** and **Poll ShipPDF for Result**.\n- In **Post Datasheet to ShipPDF**, set your `template_id` and map the `data` fields to your datasheet template's data schema (product name, model, SKU, description, specifications).\n- Connect **Google Sheets** and **Google Drive** credentials and point the trigger at your product sheet.\n\n### Notes\n\n- **Credits:** one ShipPDF credit per datasheet. The `Idempotency-Key` **header** makes retries safe (a replay returns the original document, no double charge).\n- **Product photo (optional):** if your template's image node is bound to data, map an `image_url` column \u2014 ShipPDF image nodes accept `{ type: url }`. Otherwise keep the photo in the template and drop the field.\n- **Failures:** invalid data is rejected at the generate step with HTTP 422 before any credit; render/billing failures arrive as `status: failed` on the poll.\n- **Write back to your sheet (optional):** add a Google Sheets *Update row* node after *Save Datasheet to Drive* to write the Drive link into a `Datasheet URL` column, so each product row carries a shareable datasheet.\n\n### Customization\n\nSwap the trigger (Airtable, a PIM, a form), add the product photo, or change the specification mapping to fit your catalog.\n\nFree ShipPDF API key \u2192 https://shippdf.com"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "d0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
      "name": "Section: capture",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        192,
        80
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 240,
        "height": 300,
        "content": "## Capture new product\n\nStarts when a new product row is added to the Google Sheet catalog."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "d0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
      "name": "Section: generate-poll",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1040,
        112
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 720,
        "height": 380,
        "content": "## Generate and poll for datasheet\n\nSends the product data to ShipPDF, then polls `GET /v1/documents/{id}` every 3s until the PDF is ready. Anything still processing loops back to the wait. No public callback URL needed."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "d0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004",
      "name": "Section: check",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1800,
        80
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 432,
        "height": 460,
        "content": "## Check result\n\nRoutes a completed datasheet to archiving and a failed one to the alert placeholder."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "d0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000005",
      "name": "Section: archive",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1800,
        -220
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 480,
        "height": 260,
        "content": "## Archive datasheet\n\nDownloads the completed PDF and stores a copy in Google Drive. Add a Sheets *Update row* node here to write the link back to the catalog."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
